"Weighted Seshadri constants and ellipsoid embeddings (https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.27574)\nciteturn2academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Title: Weighted Seshadri constants and ellipsoid embeddings\nTitle: Weighted Seshadri constants and ellipsoid embeddings\nAuthors: Jonathan David Evans\nDate: Tue May 26 18:47:25 2026\n\nWe explore Seshadri constants associated to weighted blow-ups of complex projective varieties and demonstrate how to use this notion to construct symplectic embeddings of ellipsoids. We illustrate the utility of this point of view by providing constructions of full fillings of $\\mathbb{CP}^2$ by ellipsoids corresponding to all of the exceptional (post-Fibonacci) steps of the McDuff--Schlenk staircase and some non-obvious embeddings of ellipsoids in ellipsoids.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWeighted Seshadri constants and ellipsoid embeddings (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/405371774_Weighted_Seshadri_constants_and_ellipsoid_embeddings)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: last month; # Weighted Seshadri constants and ellipsoid embeddings\n\n# Weighted Seshadri constants and ellipsoid embeddings\n\n  * May 2026\n\nDOI:10.48550/arXiv.2605.27574\n\nAuthors:\n\nJonathan David Evans\n\nJonathan David Evans\n\n\n## Abstract\n\nWe explore Seshadri constants associated to weighted blow-ups of complex projective varieties and demonstrate how to use this notion to construct symplectic embeddings of ellipsoids. We illustrate the utility of this point of view by providing constructions of full fillings of $\\mathbb{CP}^2$ by ellipsoids corresponding to all of the exceptional (post-Fibonacci) steps of the McDuff--Schlenk staircase and some non-obvious embeddings of ellipsoids in ellipsoids.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[Literature Review] Weighted Seshadri constants and ellipsoid embeddings (https://w