und and Motivation: The Gromov width of a symplectic manifold $(Z, \\omega)$ is related to its Seshadri constant, $\\text{Sesh}(Z, D, p) = \\sup{\\varepsilon : g^*D - \\varepsilon C \\text{ is ample}}$, where $g: Y \\to Z$ is the blow-up of $Z$ at point $p$, $D$ is an ample divisor, and $C$ is the exceptional divisor. This connection, established by McDuff and Polterovich, bounds the Gromov width from below. Biran extended this idea, suggesting that weighted blow-ups could be used to study symplectic embeddings of ellipsoids. A symplectic ellipsoid $E(\\sigma)$ is defined as $E(\\sigma) = {z \\in \\mathbb{C}^n : \\sum_{j=1}^n \\frac{|z_j|^2}{\\sigma_j} \\leq 1}$. The seminal work of McDuff and Schlenk fully characterized which ellipsoids embed into $\\mathbb{CP}^2$, revealing a \"staircase\" of packing ratios that includes infinitely many Fibonacci-related steps and nine \"exceptional steps.\" Existing methods, such as symplectic inflation, are often intricate and require careful attention to local models of inflationary curves. This paper aims to bypass inflation, using the Nakai–Moishezon criterion for ampleness directly.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n重み付きSeshadri定数と楕円体埋込み〖JST機械翻訳〗 | 文献情報 | J-GLOBAL 科学技術総合リンクセンター (https://jglobal.jst.go.jp/detail?JGLOBAL_ID=202602200299458914)\nciteturn2search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Weighted Seshadri constants and ellipsoid embeddings\n\nプレプリント\n\nJ-GLOBAL ID：202602200299458914   整理番号：26P0159003\n\n# 重み付きSeshadri定数と楕円体埋込み〖JST機械翻訳〗\n\nWeighted Seshadri constants and ellipsoid embeddings\n\n  * 出版者サイト {{ this.onShowPLink() }} 複写サービスで全文入手\n  * このテーマを更に深掘りする（JDreamⅢへ）\n\nこの文献はプレプリントです。プレプリントについてはこちらをご確認ください。\n\narXiv掲載論文の撤回有無については、一次情報をご確認下さい。\n\n著者 (1件)：\n\nEvans Jonathan David\n\nEvans Jonathan David について\n\n  * 「Evans Jonathan David」ですべてを検索\n\n資料名：\n\narXiv\n\narXiv について\n\n  * JST資料番号 O7000B ですべてを検索\n\n発行年： 2026年06月05日  プレプリントサーバーでの情